Based on the search results, I found relevant information about creating servlets in Liferay OSGi modules using the whiteboard pattern.

An example of creating a servlet in a Liferay OSGi module uses the `@Component` annotation with properties like `osgi.http.whiteboard.context.path=/`, `osgi.http.whiteboard.servlet.name`, and `osgi.http.whiteboard.servlet.pattern` to define the servlet configuration.

The servlet class extends HttpServlet and is registered as a service:

```java
@Component(
    immediate = true,
    property = {
        "osgi.http.whiteboard.context.path=/",
        "osgi.http.whiteboard.servlet.name=my.package.name.myTest",
        "osgi.http.whiteboard.servlet.pattern=/myTest/test",
    },
    service = Servlet.class
)
public class myTest extends HttpServlet {
    // servlet implementation
}
```

While the search results don't contain specific examples using the exact property `osgi.http.whiteboard.context.select` with `(osgi.http.whiteboard.context.name=default)` that you mentioned, the pattern shown above demonstrates how to configure servlets using the OSGi Whiteboard Servlet specification in Liferay. The `osgi.http.whiteboard.context.select` property would be used to target a specific servlet context by name rather than creating a new one.


